 Open sessions are not held across view rendering (`spring.jpa.open-in-view` is disabled), so associations that a view needs are fetched eagerly at the mapping level.
 
+**Veterinarian reads and the `vets` cache.** Narrowing the veterinarian directory by specialty is a repository query, not a filter over a fetched collection, so the page is cut from the narrowed result. The narrowed query carries no `@Cacheable`; the two unnarrowed reads keep theirs ([ADR: The Specialty-Narrowed Veterinarian Query Is Not Cached](adr/2026-08-05-uncached-specialty-narrowed-vet-query.md)). Matching folds case inside the query rather than relying on column collation, so it behaves identically on all three vendors — unlike owner search, whose case sensitivity varies by vendor ([Known Defects](#known-defects)).
+
 ## Dependency Policy
 
 Minimize external dependencies. Every dependency is an attack surface and a maintenance burden.
